{
  "source": "captions:manual",
  "model": null,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 11.37,
      "end": 12.99,
      "text": "I think that once you learn",
      "id": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 12.99,
      "end": 14.91,
      "text": "about the second law of thermodynamics,",
      "id": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 14.91,
      "end": 16.8,
      "text": "it can be a little depressing.",
      "id": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 16.8,
      "end": 17.633,
      "text": "You've been told",
      "id": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 17.633,
      "end": 19.98,
      "text": "that there's a fundamental feature of reality:",
      "id": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 19.98,
      "end": 22.29,
      "text": "that disorder increases,",
      "id": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 22.29,
      "end": 24.69,
      "text": "that things just wind down, right?",
      "id": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 24.69,
      "end": 26.52,
      "text": "That batteries run out,",
      "id": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 26.52,
      "end": 28.29,
      "text": "that cream and coffee mix together,",
      "id": 8
    },
    {
      "start": 28.29,
      "end": 29.88,
      "text": "that ice cubes melt.",
      "id": 9
    },
    {
      "start": 29.88,
      "end": 33.45,
      "text": "It's kind of a depressing view of the future.",
      "id": 10
    },
    {
      "start": 33.45,
      "end": 35.97,
      "text": "How did all of this interestingness",
      "id": 11
    },
    {
      "start": 35.97,
      "end": 37.83,
      "text": "come about in the first place?",
      "id": 12
    },
    {
      "start": 37.83,
      "end": 41.01,
      "text": "If the whole thing that reality does",
      "id": 13
    },
    {
      "start": 41.01,
      "end": 44.91,
      "text": "is just move closer and closer to complete disorder,",
      "id": 14
    },
    {
      "start": 44.91,
      "end": 47.91,
      "text": "then how did something as exquisitely organized",
      "id": 15
    },
    {
      "start": 47.91,
      "end": 49.983,
      "text": "as a human being come about?",
      "id": 16
    },
    {
      "start": 52.71,
      "end": 55.32,
      "text": "This idea that there's this tension",
      "id": 17
    },
    {
      "start": 55.32,
      "end": 58.5,
      "text": "between the organization of things in the Universe",
      "id": 18
    },
    {
      "start": 58.5,
      "end": 61.38,
      "text": "and the natural evolution of things",
      "id": 19
    },
    {
      "start": 61.38,
      "end": 63.09,
      "text": "became a little bit sharper",
      "id": 20
    },
    {
      "start": 63.09,
      "end": 64.74,
      "text": "over the course of the 1800s",
      "id": 21
    },
    {
      "start": 64.74,
      "end": 66.66,
      "text": "because that's when we put together",
      "id": 22
    },
    {
      "start": 66.66,
      "end": 69.69,
      "text": "this idea that entropy increases all the time.",
      "id": 23
    },
    {
      "start": 69.69,
      "end": 72.93,
      "text": "Things tend to go from orderly to disorderly",
      "id": 24
    },
    {
      "start": 72.93,
      "end": 76.5,
      "text": "just because there are many more ways to be disorderly.",
      "id": 25
    },
    {
      "start": 76.5,
      "end": 79.83,
      "text": "This is a deep down law of nature.",
      "id": 26
    },
    {
      "start": 79.83,
      "end": 83.03999999999999,
      "text": "It implies what we call the 'Heat death of the Universe':",
      "id": 27
    },
    {
      "start": 83.03999999999999,
      "end": 84.69,
      "text": "that all the stuff you see,",
      "id": 28
    },
    {
      "start": 84.69,
      "end": 87.99,
      "text": "the engines, the burning stars, the living beings,",
      "id": 29
    },
    {
      "start": 87.99,
      "end": 92.19,
      "text": "these all represent systems that are increasing",
      "id": 30
    },
    {
      "start": 92.19,
      "end": 94.08,
      "text": "the overall entropy of the Universe.",
      "id": 31
    },
    {
      "start": 94.08,
      "end": 96.99000000000001,
      "text": "And if you think, which is probably true,",
      "id": 32
    },
    {
      "start": 96.99000000000001,
      "end": 99.78,
      "text": "that there's a maximum entropy you can reach,",
      "id": 33
    },
    {
      "start": 99.78,
      "end": 103.14,
      "text": "a maximum level of disorderliness and chaos,",
      "id": 34
    },
    {
      "start": 103.14,
      "end": 104.58,
      "text": "eventually we will get there",
      "id": 35
    },
    {
      "start": 104.58,
      "end": 108.36,
      "text": "and all the interestingness in the Universe will be gone.",
      "id": 36
    },
    {
      "start": 108.36,
      "end": 111.18,
      "text": "The Universe will reach what we call an 'equilibrium':",
      "id": 37
    },
    {
      "start": 111.18,
      "end": 113.16,
      "text": "a state of maximum chaos",
      "id": 38
    },
    {
      "start": 113.16,
      "end": 116.31,
      "text": "and nothing interesting happening anymore.",
      "id": 39
    },
    {
      "start": 116.31,
      "end": 119.07,
      "text": "One of the issues with really feeling",
      "id": 40
    },
    {
      "start": 119.07,
      "end": 121.65,
      "text": "through the implications of the second law of thermodynamics",
      "id": 41
    },
    {
      "start": 121.65,
      "end": 126.36,
      "text": "is that people tend to mix up simple versus complex",
      "id": 42
    },
    {
      "start": 126.36,
      "end": 128.22,
      "text": "and orderly versus disorderly.",
      "id": 43
    },
    {
      "start": 128.22,
      "end": 130.59,
      "text": "The truth is these are two different axes,",
      "id": 44
    },
    {
      "start": 130.59,
      "end": 133.2,
      "text": "two different ways of thinking about something.",
      "id": 45
    },
    {
      "start": 133.2,
      "end": 134.49,
      "text": "The increase of entropy",
      "id": 46
    },
    {
      "start": 134.49,
      "end": 136.86,
      "text": "says that we go from orderly to disorderly,",
      "id": 47
    },
    {
      "start": 136.86,
      "end": 140.37,
      "text": "but it says nothing about simple versus complex.",
      "id": 48
    },
    {
      "start": 140.37,
      "end": 142.53,
      "text": "This is a new scientific question",
      "id": 49
    },
    {
      "start": 142.53,
      "end": 144.6,
      "text": "that we are facing right now:",
      "id": 50
    },
    {
      "start": 144.6,
      "end": 149.6,
      "text": "'What is the journey from low entropy to high entropy like",
      "id": 51
    },
    {
      "start": 150.21,
      "end": 152.85,
      "text": "and how is it affected by the laws of physics",
      "id": 52
    },
    {
      "start": 152.85,
      "end": 156.21,
      "text": "so that the actual path it takes",
      "id": 53
    },
    {
      "start": 156.21,
      "end": 158.823,
      "text": "leads to complex structures?'",
      "id": 54
    },
    {
      "start": 161.07,
      "end": 163.07999999999998,
      "text": "One of the difficulties in figuring out,",
      "id": 55
    },
    {
      "start": 163.07999999999998,
      "end": 166.77,
      "text": "specifically, how life here on Earth came into being",
      "id": 56
    },
    {
      "start": 166.77,
      "end": 169.62,
      "text": "is that it's not just a random sort of complex system.",
      "id": 57
    },
    {
      "start": 169.62,
      "end": 171.36,
      "text": "It's a very specific thing.",
      "id": 58
    },
    {
      "start": 171.36,
      "end": 174.81,
      "text": "And life as we know it now involves different aspects,",
      "id": 59
    },
    {
      "start": 174.81,
      "end": 176.37,
      "text": "all of which are important.",
      "id": 60
    },
    {
      "start": 176.37,
      "end": 178.5,
      "text": "You need replication, right?",
      "id": 61
    },
    {
      "start": 178.5,
      "end": 179.79,
      "text": "You need Darwinian evolution.",
      "id": 62
    },
    {
      "start": 179.79,
      "end": 180.93,
      "text": "We have DNA.",
      "id": 63
    },
    {
      "start": 180.93,
      "end": 183.54,
      "text": "We have a genome that gets replicated,",
      "id": 64
    },
    {
      "start": 183.54,
      "end": 185.52,
      "text": "not perfectly, but pretty well.",
      "id": 65
    },
    {
      "start": 185.52,
      "end": 187.56,
      "text": "You need compartmentalization.",
      "id": 66
    },
    {
      "start": 187.56,
      "end": 189.45,
      "text": "Every cell has a cell wall",
      "id": 67
    },
    {
      "start": 189.45,
      "end": 191.34,
      "text": "so you can separate the living cell",
      "id": 68
    },
    {
      "start": 191.34,
      "end": 192.81,
      "text": "from the rest of the world.",
      "id": 69
    },
    {
      "start": 192.81,
      "end": 194.82,
      "text": "And also you need metabolism, right?",
      "id": 70
    },
    {
      "start": 194.82,
      "end": 195.9,
      "text": "You need that fuel,",
      "id": 71
    },
    {
      "start": 195.9,
      "end": 197.94,
      "text": "you need that low-entropy energy",
      "id": 72
    },
    {
      "start": 197.94,
      "end": 199.8,
      "text": "that we can use to keep ourselves going",
      "id": 73
    },
    {
      "start": 199.8,
      "end": 203.19,
      "text": "and then expel to the world in a higher-entropy form.",
      "id": 74
    },
    {
      "start": 203.19,
      "end": 205.35,
      "text": "So, which came first?",
      "id": 75
    },
    {
      "start": 205.35,
      "end": 208.95,
      "text": "This is why explaining the beginning of complex structures",
      "id": 76
    },
    {
      "start": 208.95,
      "end": 209.78300000000002,
      "text": "is always hard,",
      "id": 77
    },
    {
      "start": 209.78300000000002,
      "end": 212.55,
      "text": "because they all seem to depend on each other.",
      "id": 78
    },
    {
      "start": 212.55,
      "end": 215.37,
      "text": "There is a replication-first camp",
      "id": 79
    },
    {
      "start": 215.37,
      "end": 218.513,
      "text": "in the origin of life studies literature that says,",
      "id": 80
    },
    {
      "start": 218.513,
      "end": 222.09,
      "text": "\"Look, clearly the genetic information is necessary",
      "id": 81
    },
    {
      "start": 222.09,
      "end": 223.47,
      "text": "to call it life,",
      "id": 82
    },
    {
      "start": 223.47,
      "end": 224.57999999999998,
      "text": "that must have come first",
      "id": 83
    },
    {
      "start": 224.57999999999998,
      "end": 226.71,
      "text": "and it must have hooked up to an energy source.\"",
      "id": 84
    },
    {
      "start": 226.71,
      "end": 229.59300000000002,
      "text": "But there's also a metabolism-first camp that says,",
      "id": 85
    },
    {
      "start": 229.59300000000002,
      "end": 230.901,
      "text": "\"Look, it doesn't matter",
      "id": 86
    },
    {
      "start": 230.901,
      "end": 232.38,
      "text": "if you have information sitting there,",
      "id": 87
    },
    {
      "start": 232.38,
      "end": 234.93,
      "text": "if it's not going someplace, if it's not doing anything,",
      "id": 88
    },
    {
      "start": 234.93,
      "end": 237.48,
      "text": "if it's not moving around and metabolizing,",
      "id": 89
    },
    {
      "start": 237.48,
      "end": 239.28,
      "text": "you can't call it life.\"",
      "id": 90
    },
    {
      "start": 239.28,
      "end": 240.42,
      "text": "And the nice thing to me",
      "id": 91
    },
    {
      "start": 240.42,
      "end": 242.61,
      "text": "about the metabolism-first point of view",
      "id": 92
    },
    {
      "start": 242.61,
      "end": 246.12,
      "text": "is that you can kind of see how it might arise",
      "id": 93
    },
    {
      "start": 246.12,
      "end": 250.53,
      "text": "out of purely physical, non-biological processes",
      "id": 94
    },
    {
      "start": 250.53,
      "end": 253.41,
      "text": "because remember, to maintain its orderliness",
      "id": 95
    },
    {
      "start": 253.41,
      "end": 254.76,
      "text": "and its complexity,",
      "id": 96
    },
    {
      "start": 254.76,
      "end": 258.36,
      "text": "living beings need to increase the entropy of the Universe,",
      "id": 97
    },
    {
      "start": 258.36,
      "end": 261.963,
      "text": "they need to feed off of low-entropy energy.",
      "id": 98
    },
    {
      "start": 262.98,
      "end": 264.0,
      "text": "So this was an idea",
      "id": 99
    },
    {
      "start": 264.0,
      "end": 267.3,
      "text": "that a number of biologists and geologists had.",
      "id": 100
    },
    {
      "start": 267.3,
      "end": 269.58,
      "text": "And on the basis of it, they made predictions.",
      "id": 101
    },
    {
      "start": 269.58,
      "end": 270.51,
      "text": "They said, you know,",
      "id": 102
    },
    {
      "start": 270.51,
      "end": 273.27,
      "text": "\"Life is not gonna form in some warm pond.\"",
      "id": 103
    },
    {
      "start": 273.27,
      "end": 274.53,
      "text": "This was Darwin's idea,",
      "id": 104
    },
    {
      "start": 274.53,
      "end": 276.15,
      "text": "that maybe you just put all the stuff together,",
      "id": 105
    },
    {
      "start": 276.15,
      "end": 276.983,
      "text": "all the ingredients,",
      "id": 106
    },
    {
      "start": 276.983,
      "end": 280.38,
      "text": "and eventually a little bug crawls out, okay?",
      "id": 107
    },
    {
      "start": 280.38,
      "end": 281.82,
      "text": "Or a little bacterium.",
      "id": 108
    },
    {
      "start": 281.82,
      "end": 283.53,
      "text": "And they said, \"Look, that's never gonna happen,",
      "id": 109
    },
    {
      "start": 283.53,
      "end": 286.11,
      "text": "because there's no increasing entropy.",
      "id": 110
    },
    {
      "start": 286.11,
      "end": 287.01,
      "text": "What you need is",
      "id": 111
    },
    {
      "start": 287.01,
      "end": 290.85,
      "text": "just the right biochemical, geological arrangement of things",
      "id": 112
    },
    {
      "start": 290.85,
      "end": 294.45,
      "text": "to have these long, sophisticated, complex reactions happen",
      "id": 113
    },
    {
      "start": 294.45,
      "end": 298.59000000000003,
      "text": "that can then be captured into the first living organism.\"",
      "id": 114
    },
    {
      "start": 298.59000000000003,
      "end": 299.67,
      "text": "And they thought about",
      "id": 115
    },
    {
      "start": 299.67,
      "end": 302.67,
      "text": "what kind of conditions would they be,",
      "id": 116
    },
    {
      "start": 302.67,
      "end": 306.54,
      "text": "and they thought that it might be a warm, hydrothermal vent",
      "id": 117
    },
    {
      "start": 306.54,
      "end": 308.1,
      "text": "under the oceans, right?",
      "id": 118
    },
    {
      "start": 308.1,
      "end": 309.93,
      "text": "With certain chemical balances.",
      "id": 119
    },
    {
      "start": 309.93,
      "end": 310.763,
      "text": "And I'm a physicist,",
      "id": 120
    },
    {
      "start": 310.763,
      "end": 312.81,
      "text": "I don't know the details and I shouldn't say anything,",
      "id": 121
    },
    {
      "start": 312.81,
      "end": 315.96,
      "text": "but the point is these kinds of hydrothermal vents",
      "id": 122
    },
    {
      "start": 315.96,
      "end": 317.82,
      "text": "were not known at the time,",
      "id": 123
    },
    {
      "start": 317.82,
      "end": 319.53,
      "text": "they had not yet been discovered,",
      "id": 124
    },
    {
      "start": 319.53,
      "end": 321.15,
      "text": "but a prediction was made-",
      "id": 125
    },
    {
      "start": 321.15,
      "end": 322.8,
      "text": "these must exist",
      "id": 126
    },
    {
      "start": 322.8,
      "end": 325.38,
      "text": "in order for life to have come into existence.",
      "id": 127
    },
    {
      "start": 325.38,
      "end": 328.53,
      "text": "And after the prediction was made, we found them.",
      "id": 128
    },
    {
      "start": 328.53,
      "end": 330.72,
      "text": "Famously, the 'Lost City' formation",
      "id": 129
    },
    {
      "start": 330.72,
      "end": 332.43,
      "text": "at the bottom of the Atlantic Ocean",
      "id": 130
    },
    {
      "start": 332.43,
      "end": 334.14,
      "text": "was found by submersibles",
      "id": 131
    },
    {
      "start": 334.14,
      "end": 336.42,
      "text": "going down near the bottom of the ocean floor.",
      "id": 132
    },
    {
      "start": 336.42,
      "end": 339.18,
      "text": "They found exactly the kind of geochemical conditions",
      "id": 133
    },
    {
      "start": 339.18,
      "end": 340.8,
      "text": "that had been hypothesized",
      "id": 134
    },
    {
      "start": 340.8,
      "end": 343.59000000000003,
      "text": "as possible places where life could have formed.",
      "id": 135
    },
    {
      "start": 343.59000000000003,
      "end": 345.24,
      "text": "Does that mean it's right?",
      "id": 136
    },
    {
      "start": 345.24,
      "end": 347.04,
      "text": "No, but it's a little bit of evidence",
      "id": 137
    },
    {
      "start": 347.04,
      "end": 349.17,
      "text": "that it could be on the right track.",
      "id": 138
    },
    {
      "start": 349.17,
      "end": 351.45,
      "text": "The origin of life, I think, personally,",
      "id": 139
    },
    {
      "start": 351.45,
      "end": 355.11,
      "text": "is one of the most important unanswered scientific questions",
      "id": 140
    },
    {
      "start": 355.11,
      "end": 356.55,
      "text": "but it's one that we're absolutely",
      "id": 141
    },
    {
      "start": 356.55,
      "end": 358.08299999999997,
      "text": "making progress on right now.",
      "id": 142
    },
    {
      "start": 360.15,
      "end": 361.59,
      "text": "Get smarter, faster",
      "id": 143
    },
    {
      "start": 361.59,
      "end": 364.71,
      "text": "with videos from the world's biggest thinkers.",
      "id": 144
    },
    {
      "start": 364.71,
      "end": 367.35,
      "text": "And to learn even more from the world's biggest thinkers,",
      "id": 145
    },
    {
      "start": 367.35,
      "end": 369.543,
      "text": "get Big Think+ for your business.",
      "id": 146
    }
  ],
  "duration": 371.0,
  "elapsed_s": 0.0,
  "real_time_factor": 0.0,
  "language": "en"
}